    "result_text": "All 263 tests pass with `BUILD SUCCESS`, including the acceptance test `coreReturnsUnifiedMemberId`. (The `ERROR`/`WARN` lines in the earlier output are expected noise from tests that deliberately exercise error paths.)\n\n## Summary\n\nUnified `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` into a single `memberId` formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`, and removed the derived `checkDigit` field.\n\n**New member-id generation** \u2014 `AssignMemberId.java` (replaces the deleted `AssignCustomerCode.java` and `AssignMembershipNumber.java`) builds `memberId` in one step:\n- `REGION` \u2014 postcode \u2192 city \u2192 `UNKNOWN` (unchanged region logic)\n- `FY` \u2014 2-digit fiscal year of `registrationDate` (fiscal year starts 1 July)\n- `HASH8` \u2014 first 8 upper-hex of SHA-256 over `normalizedTelephone + lastName` (same hash as the region-and-hash identity)\n- `CHK` \u2014 a single Luhn check digit over the digits of `<REGION><FY><HASH8>`\n- **Collision handling** now dedups on `memberId`, appending `-<n>` (smallest n \u2265 2).\n\n**Pipeline** (`owners.POST.yml`) \u2014 `build \u2192 assignMemberId \u2192 \u2026`, with the old `assignMembershipNumber` step removed so `capMembershipLevel \u2192 save`.\n\n**Field removal & references:**\n- `Owner.java` \u2014 `customerCode`/`membershipNumber` fields+accessors replaced by `memberId`; the four DB schemas (hsqldb/h2/mysql/postgres) drop `customer_code`/`membership_number` for a single `member_id` column (VARCHAR(32)/TEXT to fit the longer id + collision suffix).\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 `customerCode`, `checkDigit`, `membershipNumber` schema entries replaced by a single `memberId` (drives the generated `OwnerDto`).\n- `OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 removed the `checkDigit` mapping+method; `locality` now reads the REGION prefix from `memberId`, `fiscalYear` reads the FY segment from `memberId` (both keep a fallback for pre-existing/seed owners without a `memberId`, so `ownerSegment` \u2014 which depends on `locality` \u2014 references `memberId` too); `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` ignores `memberId`.\n- Audit \u2014 `AuditOwnerCreated` logs `memberId`, and `OwnerCreatedEvent`'s identifier field is renamed to `memberId`.\n\nThe fiscal-year value, audit record, and owner segment now all reference `memberId`, as specified.",
